ll night  for high school graduates a park  security guard apparently saw him and  called at him to get down but he was  still on the track when the tram struck  him and dragged him under its for  carriages following the passing there  were reports that the spectral figure is  sometimes seen at night around the  monorail track some say they've seen him  running alongside the trains while  others say that whenever a tram  approaches the monorail  ghost vanishes Debby stone a Disneyland  employee was tragically crushed in 1974  while working at the park  Debbie stone was 18 years old when she  was a hostess at the America sings  attraction she got caught between the  rotating wall and the stage wall in the  theater various changes were made  afterward to stop such a tragic event  from ever occurring again the solid  walls were replaced with a breakaway  ones a safety light was put in to warn  the operator when anyone got too close  to the area and it said that after her  passing  Debbie herself played a part and keeping  other safe cast members who worked on  the attraction are said to have heard a  voice telling them to be careful when  they got too close to the walls  the attraction eventually closed in the  late 80s we hope Debbie was then able to  rest in peace knowing that no one else  would be subject to the same fate as her  it's reassuring to hear a haunting  theory that involves a Friendly Ghost  Regina dolly young a 48 year old visitor  to Disneyland was fatally hurt when she  was hit by another bobsled after she  fell from her seat while riding the  Matterhorn in 1984 Regina yongku is  known as dolly had an unbuckled seatbelt  when she fell it's not known why she  wasn't safely harnessed in but there are  theories that she had unbuckled herself  to check on a child who was sitting  alone in the front seat dolly was alone  in the back seat this idea of dolly  watching over others has extended into  the ghost story that grew out of her  tragic fate while doing their routine  walkthroughs of the ride at the end of  the day some cast members have claimed  it felt like something was watching them  and a former cast member who worked at  Disney Land as an attractions hostess in  the early 90s said the uneasy feeling  she got was always worse in the big  cavern in the middle of the ride where  dolly died while it's impossible to  prove something like this what is a fact  is at the area on the track where the  accident happened became known as  Dolly's death these three real-life  tragic events have all resulted in  haunting theories let us know in the  comments which ghostly apparition you  think sounds most convincing it's now  time to move on to all those urban  legends lady in white if ever there's an  iconic haunting figure it's the alleged  woman in white and Disneyland has its  very own lady in white she supposedly  been spa  walking along Main Street wandering past  the stores you might be thinking that a  woman wearing all white doesn't  necessarily have to be a ghost but this  lady in white seems to hark back to the  olden times and she's wearing clothing  from the early 1900's and legend has it  that she died on the site at the turn of  the 20th century before the park was  even built but she never left the  property and stayed after the rides  arrived one theory is that she never  left because she liked the old fashioned  feel of Main Street  this ghostly apparition dressed in the  Victorian outfit does more than just  walk around though it said she actually  helps lost children find their way to  guest services to be reunited with their  parents at least this ghost isn't one  that makes you turn away in horror  there's another friendly apparition that  likes to chat with modern day visitors  let's meet him now  mr. one way Space Mountain is one of the  most famous attractions at Disneyland  and mr. one-way is one of the most  talked-about ghost stories like other  urban legends this one has many  variations which