ng theories let's delve deeper  haunted ride theories this little boy  isn't the only ghost that said to haunt  the Haunted Mansion  when it was being built in the 60s a  sound designer reportedly heard music  coming from behind a wall in the seance  room after hearing it for days he masked  to the spooky sound by putting the  speaker near it there were also rumors  amongst cast members that the spell book  in seance circle was real apparently  each morning cast members would find the  book in a different place to where it  had been left to the night before that's  not the only object that's said to be  haunted how about a whole cast of  figurines it's a small world  this one is a case of truth being  stranger than fiction or actually  inspiring fiction the author Ridley  Pearson published a series of books  called the Kingdom Keepers which were  set in the Disney parks these thrillers  are pretty freaky and one scary scene  was actually inspired by a real-life  experiences of the authors when Disney  invited him to write a thriller set  inside the theme parks really insisted  he'd have to have full access to them at  night so a Disney Imagineer showed him  around when the park was closed one  night when he was writing it's a small  world when all the power was off he saw  - animatronic dolls move and that  inspired the scene in his first book  when all of the dolls start moving he  takes things even further by having the  dolls bite at kids there's also a theory  among cast members that some of the  previous employees who worked on it's a  small world loved it so much they came  back to live there after they died the  story goes that the lights turn on and  off and the dolls will keep on dancing  and singing after the electricity has  been  turned off pirates of the Caribbean if  you thought that was a spooky tale about  ghostly props just wait until you hear  about the Pirates of the Caribbean ride  you'd assume that the bones and  skeletons used in the set for this  popular ride were fake right actual real  bones were used as props in the  Disneyland ride when it was built in  1967 it was the late pride that Walt  Disney himself supervised more on him  later  although Walt loved it to the design  team was disappointed when the faux  skeletons of the period didn't live up  to their realism of the rest of the  experience they found that fake bones  were too unconvincing so they did what  any imagined air would do and got some  actual skeletons from their friends at  UCLA Medical Center's anatomy department  the new generation of Imagineers  eventually found realistic fakes and  replaced the real ones which were then  given a proper burial but some people  including former Disney employees  insists that a few of the real deals  still remain such as the skull and the  crossbones  set over the dead captain's bed as if  that wasn't enough there's also a theory  that there's a boy ghost that can be  seen in the control tower caught on  surveillance cameras if this is true at  least they claim is that he always seems  to be happy and enjoying himself all  rumors claim Walt Disney's ghost haunts  the Disney gallery above pirates the  theory goes that the gallery was  originally designed to be Walt's  personal apartment since the one above  the main street fire station was on the  small side Walt Disney speaking of the  man himself it's now time for the final  ghosts that is said to haunt Disneyland  and we've saved the best or most famous  to last allegedly his old second-floor  apartment above the firehouse is the  location for his haunting ways he used  to stay there when visiting the park and  he would let everyone know he was there  by lighting a lamp in the window Disney  Legend has taken this story and run with  it all the way to a theory that Walt's  ghost still resides there now after he  died a cleaner was in the apartment when  she noticed the lamp was lit she turned  it off and left but when she got outside  she noticed i